    "text": {
     "en": "Globalisation means countries are linked through trade, investment and technology. It grew after 1991 when India liberalised its economy with reforms such as lower import duties and freer private investment.\nInternational trade is the exchange of goods and services among countries, and the World Trade Organisation (WTO) sets rules. Multinational companies set up plants in many countries. Foreign direct investment (FDI) brings money and skills.\nGlobalisation gives choice, jobs and technology, but small producers face tough competition. A balance of trade and wise policy protect local industry."
    }
